        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8616819aaaa148a5826f4fda0c8cbf2c",
      "statement": "The OpenWiki generation step is `continue-on-error: true`, so even a failed run deletes the transient run-state file and still opens the openwiki/update pull request preserving the pages completed before the failure, while a final step re-raises the failure with `exit 1` when the step outcome is 'failure'.",
